{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"superior-pinelike-garpike","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Summary\nThe scheduled **Live External Integration** run on 2026-08-17 (run 32000764439, job \"jira DC harness smoke (real Jira Data Center, ephemeral)\") failed\n`tests/external/live_jira_dc/test_multi_project_rehearsal.py::test_unknown_project_fails_closed`\nwith:\n\n```\nE   Failed: DID NOT RAISE RebarError\n```\n\nThe scenario maps an unknown project key — `rebar.bridge_projects_set(unknown, [\"rebar-ghost\"], repo_root=str(work))` — and then previews/syncs it, expecting the bridge to **fail closed** (RAISE `RebarError`) rather than silently no-op on an unknown mapped key. Against the live DC instance it did **not** raise.\n\n## Regression window\nThis is a NEW regression, not a long-standing failure:\n- 2026-08-15 run 31879125045 (jira DC job 94999114642): **73 passed, 1 xfailed, 0 failed**.\n- 2026-08-17 run 32000764439: **2 failed, 71 passed, 1 xfailed** — this test is one of the two new failures.\n\nSo a change landed between 2026-08-15 and 2026-08-17 that broke the fail-closed guard for an unknown bridge-project key. Candidate areas to bisect: `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/projects_store.py` (`resolve_project` / `compute_snapshot`), `bridge_projects_set`, and the multi-project preview/sync path (cf. related bug 3b87 `resolve_project` tri-state collapse, and epic 0e68 / story 368f which delivered this behavior).\n\n## Impact\nThe multi-project bridge's fail-closed safety guarantee is not holding against a real Jira DC instance: an unknown mapped project key produces a silent empty fetch/sync instead of an error. Correctness/safety of the many-to-many bridge.\n\n## The regression escaped because only a LIVE test covered it\nPer triage guidance: a live-external regression must be reproducible by a NON-external test so CI catches it without the (slow, credentialed) live suite. Today the only coverage is the live DC rehearsal.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A **RED** non-external test (unit or fake-transport integration, no live DC/creds) reproduces the regression: setting an unknown bridge-project mapping and running preview/sync RAISES `RebarError` (fail-closed) — asserted to FAIL against current `main` before the fix.\n- [ ] Root cause identified (the change between 2026-08-15 and 2026-08-17 that dropped the fail-closed behavior) and fixed so an unknown mapped project key fails closed.\n- [ ] The new non-external test passes after the fix.\n- [ ] The live rehearsal `test_unknown_project_fails_closed` passes in the next Live External Integration run.\n\n## Evidence\n- Failing run: https://github.com/navapbc/rebar/actions/runs/32000764439 (job: jira DC harness smoke)\n- Test: `tests/external/live_jira_dc/test_multi_project_rehearsal.py::test_unknown_project_fails_closed`\n- Delivered by story 368f (gasolinic-microbian-puffin), epic 0e68 (outrageous-uncultured-wildebeast).","id":"f643-db7d-3d9c-4bd3","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Live Jira DC rehearsal: unknown bridge project no longer fails closed (test_unknown_project_fails_closed — DID NOT RAISE RebarError)"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786994077943346001,"uuid":"f10e7bd9-337a-4c0e-b56d-cfae4db1e346"}